  "result": "Perfect! All 164 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Created `src/dates.js` with UTC-based date utilities:**\n\n**`isValidDate(text)` function:**\n- Validates YYYY-MM-DD format exactly\n- Checks that the date is real (no Feb 30, etc.)\n- Returns `false` for non-strings or bad formats\n- All validation uses UTC to avoid timezone issues\n- Handles leap years correctly (Feb 29 in 2024, 2020, 2000 \u2192 valid; 2023, 1900, 2001 \u2192 invalid)\n\n**`addDays(date, n)` function:**\n- Adds `n` days to a YYYY-MM-DD date string\n- Supports negative numbers (subtract days)\n- All arithmetic in UTC (no timezone quirks)\n- Handles month/year boundaries correctly\n- Returns result as YYYY-MM-DD string\n\n**`daysBetween(a, b)` function:**\n- Calculates `b - a` in whole days\n- Returns positive for dates moving forward, negative backward\n- All arithmetic in UTC\n- Example: `daysBetween('2024-01-01', '2024-01-10')` \u2192 `9`\n\n**Updated `createInvoice()`:**\n- Now uses `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed duplicate validation logic\n- Single source of truth for date validation\n\n**Added 21 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Valid dates (various years/months)\n- Invalid formats (wrong separators, wrong order, etc.)\n- Impossible dates (Feb 30, Apr 31, etc.)\n- Leap year handling (Feb 29 in leap/non-leap years)\n- Month boundaries (Jan 31 + 1 day \u2192 Feb 1)\n- Year boundaries (Dec 31 + 1 day \u2192 Jan 1 next year)\n- Positive/negative/zero day additions\n- Large numbers (365, 366 days)\n- Forward/backward date differences\n- UTC behavior (consistent across all timezones)\n- Roundtrip operations (inverse operations work correctly)\n\nAll 164 tests pass \u2705",
